        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Iwo Jima</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">19 February – 26 March 1945</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The island of Iwo Jima in the Volcano Islands, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, with its two airfields (South Field and Central Field) and Mount Suribachi at the southern end</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-marine-corps">United States Marine Corps</a>, Navy and Army (Operation Detachment) under Admiral Raymond A. Spruance, Vice Admiral Richmond Kelly Turner, Lieutenant General Holland M. Smith and Major General Harry Schmidt, with about 60,000 Marines in the battle; the Imperial Japanese Army and Navy garrison of 21,060 men under Lieutenant General Tadamichi Kuribayashi</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Americans captured the island, which was declared secure on 26 March 1945. Of the 21,000 Japanese on the island at the start, only 216 were taken prisoner, and more than 26,000 Americans were casualties, including 6,800 dead.</span></div>
